title the bench that spoke another dialect; four reds, three closed
prompt Keaton opened Sound on the macOS bench -- read Kyri and Gauge, honor the INNER LOOP, take the widened constellation lane core-first, hold the Pond accrete-only boundary, send the twice-pulled way, stop at the custody gates.
think The roster cold read 70 guards and answered run_verdict=guard_red with three named -- ascii_comment, caravan_suite, nib_honesty -- so reds-first booked the lap before the constellation table got a look. The expansion law wants Caravan-Tally green on this bench first, and caravan_suite was one of the three, so the standfast and the core-first law pointed at the same file.
think caravan_suite named tools/ca/caravan_address_space_witness.rish, and that witness names its own answer on line two: vendor/microkit is not checked out, an environment precondition rather than a tree red, exactly as the loop seed says. git submodule update --init --recursive then failed on every path, and the reason was the host rather than the tree -- a global url.ssh://git@github.com/.insteadof https://github.com/ rewrites every public submodule to ssh, where this key has no rights, and --init --recursive aborts on the first unreachable repository and leaves the rest untouched. GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null clones each over plain https without touching the host config; all six stand, and the address-space rung reads GREEN.
think %278 is the sharper of the two dialect reds because it fails toward refusal rather than toward silence. rye_comment_ascii_scan.sh and shell_comment_ascii_scan.sh both count with awk and the regex /[^\x00-\x7F]/. The \x hex escape is GNU awk; BWK awk reads the bracket as literal characters, the negated class matches every character alive, and the living Rye reading came back 16,131,707 across 1,900 files against a ceiling of 4,338. The four-file control caught it at chars=97 where four was the answer -- and the shell control stayed green through the identical fault, because it asserts only that each planted line was counted. A control that asks whether a reading fired cannot see one that fires too often.
think The repair is POSIX octal, [^\001-\177], the same move living_card_ascii_scan.sh already made when it dropped grep -P for a C-locale byte range -- cited beside the change so two repairs read as one lesson. The proof is arithmetic rather than argument: repaired, this bench reads 4,338 across 369 files and 505 across 153, character for character the numbers the Linux pier recorded on 20260825 for the same two meters. That agreement is the cross-dialect check a second awk on this host could not give.
think %279 came from the choir's next rung: flock(1) is util-linux and macOS ships none, so tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh dies on flock: command not found and refuses without waiting -- 44 witnesses tree-wide, 7 of them Caravan. lock_acquire and lock_release join tools/fixtures/shell_portable.sh as its sixth named dialect question, built on mkdir, which is atomic on every POSIX filesystem. The one property a descriptor lock has for free is release on process death, restored by writing the owner pid inside the lock and letting a waiter that finds a dead owner reap it. The lock is renamed .build.lock.d because the elder spelling left a zero-byte FILE at .build.lock and mkdir over a plain file fails forever; a new mechanism under a new name makes that residue irrelevant with no special case.
think %280 was the card's own honesty: nib_honesty read advertised=4 gone=3 verdict=FLOATING_CLAIM, because the 20260826 deep debride rewrote the three walk-back commits out of the object store. The debride rule already refreshes the git nib after a rewrite, and that refresh reached the field with a guard rather than the class of claim the guard protects. The card now names where the record lives -- the settled decisions verbatim in construction/archive, the arcs in session-logs -- and CHECKPOINTS.md keeps every hash it wrote, since it is append-only testimony.
think %281 stays OPEN and his. The choir's third failure was caravan_answer_witness building against caravan/tally_copy.zig: FileNotFound while capabilities.zig stood beside it, and the same command alone succeeded silently. pgrep named the cause: a SECOND caravan_suite_witness (pid 24973) was singing the same 113 rungs from another session in this checkout, and rye build writes its .zig shadows beside the sources with no lock, so each build's cleanup deletes the other's mid-compile. glow_run_worker.sh books this exact lesson for its own artifacts; the driver underneath does not. A lock in bridge_to_zig or one tree per star are both Keaton's word, so it is surfaced rather than crossed.
obs Council rota N=3518 mod 5 = 3 -- Water, the row that tastes, and it read as provenance on a bench meeting the tree for the first time. Its fixed seat is the happy zone, whose thin edge already names the host's own dialect as a seam; three of this lap's four reds were exactly that seam, found up close by running rather than at a distance by reading.
obs The Pond accrete-only boundary was never approached -- no ai-jail markdown touched. The seed cadence stays Dream's, and the card's own cadence section was repaired where it still instructed a fifth-round publish the Now block says was cut.
obs The new helper ships with its own control rather than only its callers: ten lock behaviours in shell_portable_control.sh, including a held lock refusing a second holder after waiting its bound, a dead owner reaped, and an empty or non-numeric pid file waited on rather than reaped -- since reaping there would hand two holders one lock. Twenty-five behaviours pass, and shell_dialect_witness.rish repins the count in the same commit. Shipping a portable helper with no control would have booked %278's lesson without applying it.
obs %281 fired a second time before its own row landed, and the second firing is the expensive one: commit 7bd3cb949, subject construction: standfast the fusion build on the inner loop, carries this lap's entire construction/ITINERARY.md diff, because the other session committed a path this session had staged. Neither hand did anything wrong alone. The row now says so, and the card work is recorded under a subject that does not describe it -- REDS %255's shape without the amend.
obs The hot roster read five red over a tree that moved under it (tree_moved=yes), and four were mine to answer: the ledger headline drifted 277 against a measured 281, construction/REDS.md stood at 33,299 against a declared 24,576, and remember_git_nib named a card whose nib the send pins. The pin came back to 23,152 by folding %276 through %280 onto construction/archive/REDS-the-instrument-and-the-host-rows-276-280.md; %273 stayed because its own tail reads OPEN none, closed by reconstruction, and the fold reads the word rather than the sentence -- a dated row keeps its wording, so the pin keeps the row.
obs Every artifact touched carded A+ at meter with service judged 90 to 95, so no molt frame was pushed. The submodule trap became an ITINERARY directive line rather than a lap, which is where the QA stack unwinds at depth 2.
